<header><p class="enc-kicker">Institution</p><h1 class="enc-title">People's Seimas</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1940">1940</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> · Also known as People’s Seimas</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The People's <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/seimas">Seimas</a> was the parliament of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lithuania">Lithuania</a> elected on 14–15 July 1940 under Soviet occupation, in a vote with a single list of Communist-approved candidates. On 21 July it proclaimed Lithuania a Soviet socialist republic and asked to join the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/soviet-union">Soviet Union</a>, which admitted it on 3 August 1940; the assembly then became the Supreme Soviet of the Lithuanian SSR.</p></div>
